Reproduction evidence for resuming
The full report is adv-review-loop/captain-hold-round-3-result.md under this worktree's git directory.
The script is captain-hold-round-3-evidence/alarm-ownership-repro.sh in that same directory.
Run normally for the hold variant; FM_REPRO_MODE=stdout selects the independent output-failure variant.
FM_REPRO_REVISION=77190d9 selects the pre-fix regression control.
The fixture-only rm boundary invokes verified healthy recovery, five real failed auto-arm/guard cycles that deliver the replacement warning, and either a hold or closed stdout before old cleanup runs.
Observed current result: old suppressed return is 0 with no output, replacement_created=yes, replacement_alarm_retained=no; the same replacement episode then returns 0 with duplicate_warning=yes.
Pre-fix control: replacement_alarm_retained=yes; the next guard returns 2 with duplicate_warning=no.
No production file changes or timing waits are used.
